# The build context is the repository root, and the daemon receives everything
# not listed here BEFORE the first instruction runs. Without this file, `docker
# build` uploads the corpus and every checkpoint - many GB - to build an image
# that copies neither. It looks like a hung build.

# --- The expensive ones ---
data/
models/
logs/
notebooks/
benchmarks/
wandb/
.git/

# --- Local environments ---
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# --- Secrets. Belt and braces: nothing COPYs them, and they still must not
#     enter the context, because anything in the context can be read by a
#     later instruction and baked into a layer. ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
deployment/nginx/certs/
*.pem
*.key

# --- Not needed to build or run the gateway ---
tests/
docs/
seeds/
web/node_modules/
web/.next/
.github/
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.md
!README.md
